    "body": "Hmm. For some reason cuda-memcheck didn't fail on my end but looking more closely at the code that involves grid dimensions, I think I can see the problem: it seems that the kernel is being called with an incorrect number of blocks (device_buffer.size() which is the size in bytes rather than the number of blocks). Not sure why this didn't trip cuda-memcheck on my end (definitely seems like it would break all avro reads).",
